1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,902
AI can sound certain and still be wrong.

2
00:00:01,902 --> 00:00:03,805
Finly does not give it the account keys.

3
00:00:04,005 --> 00:00:07,561
Finly is a trading bot that uses real market prices and virtual money.

4
00:00:07,561 --> 00:00:09,749
AI studies the market and explains a trade.

5
00:00:09,749 --> 00:00:12,485
Fixed code caps the loss and decides what reaches Alpaca.

6
00:00:12,685 --> 00:00:15,965
When signals agree, Finly builds a paper-order plan. AI explains it;

7
00:00:15,965 --> 00:00:17,455
only rules can approve it.

8
00:00:17,655 --> 00:00:19,253
When signals conflict, Finly does nothing.

9
00:00:19,253 --> 00:00:21,384
It shows why and stops before the account.

10
00:00:21,584 --> 00:00:25,943
We tested the live options gate across 517 sampled market windows.

11
00:00:25,943 --> 00:00:29,114
A representative eligible spread had $426 maximum loss,

12
00:00:29,114 --> 00:00:32,680
below Finly's $500 limit. This is a reachability check,

13
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:33,869
not options profit.

14
00:00:34,069 --> 00:00:37,220
Finly's allocation sleeve traded during live market hours,

15
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:42,732
while its options sleeve was flat at the close rather than forcing a trade.

16
00:00:42,732 --> 00:00:48,245
Finly gained $95.32 while SPY lost $57.99—a $153.31 advantage from the same $100,000 start.

17
00:00:48,445 --> 00:00:53,676
We also replayed the allocation rule from 2013 to 2026.

18
00:00:53,676 --> 00:00:59,954
$10,000 became $106,711 with Finly—$38,629 more than SPY after modeled trading costs.

19
00:01:00,154 --> 00:01:04,823
A simpler version of the portfolio was tested on a separate 80-year market record.

20
00:01:04,823 --> 00:01:11,493
It returned 13.37% a year versus 9.48% for the market and stayed ahead across all 21 tested monthly rebalance schedules.

21
00:01:11,693 --> 00:01:14,731
Judges can inspect the 15 Alpaca ETF fill events,

22
00:01:14,731 --> 00:01:16,756
replay bullish and bearish options decisions,

23
00:01:16,756 --> 00:01:19,794
and rerun 826 automated checks in the public repository.
